  ],
  "text": "One number decides almost every energy argument, and it is energy per kilogram. It is not about ideology. It is about whether the energy fits inside the vehicle. Dry wood carries a little. Coal carries about twice that. Oil carries roughly twice coal again, and it pours, which means it pumps. A modern battery carries about one fiftieth of what the same weight of jet fuel does. Which is fine for a car, because a car sets its weight down on a road. A plane has to lift its fuel, and keep lifting it for the whole flight. Same for a ship crossing an ocean with nowhere to stop and top up. Which is why cars electrified first and aviation and shipping are still arguing. The debate is not about wanting it. It is about whether it fits. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
